<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=anji-bridge">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Building and engineering</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anji Bridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">595–605</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Zhaozhou Bridge, Great Stone Bridge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anji Bridge, or Zhaozhou Bridge, is a stone bridge over the Xiaohe River in Zhao County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, built in 595–605 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> and credited to the craftsman Li Chun; it is the world's oldest open-spandrel segmental arch bridge of stone. Its shallow arch spans 37.37 metres and saves about 40 per cent of the material a semicircular arch would need. Two small arches at each end lighten it and let floodwater through. It is the oldest standing bridge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and influenced later Chinese bridges.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anji-bridge.jpg" alt="Anji Bridge" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siyuwj · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anji_Bridge,_Zhao_County,_2020-09-06_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>595–605</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Zhao County, Hebei, China</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Li Chun · <a href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>No record from the time of its building survives; the credit to Li Chun comes from later chronicles.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/arch">Arch<span>before 3800 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=anji-bridge">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
